It's 7 minus a value: if I've understood the sources correctly,
Excalibur improves the chance by its enchantment (I think), and
wearing lenses by 2, with the total improvement capped at 5
(which results in a success rate of 1 out of 2).

A ring of searching, or the search intrinsic, or Excalibur,
provides automatic searching: you search at each move, in
addition to doing whatever the command is (which means that with
's', you search twice).  These don't cumulate, however.  Still,
when searching with 's', with a +5 or better Excalibur, you have
a 3/4 chance of success.  So 4 times will give you 99%.

Most of the time, unless you're a lawful, you'll be closer to
the 15 searchs that to the 4, however.  (And even lawfuls don't
necessarily have Excalibur at +5 or better when they need it.)

